Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||10-06-2001||05:40 PM||||Maybe the brakes are wet but I was outside washing the car with a hose and sponge.  I just drove her a little (I was parked outside the garage, sideways).  Anyway when I rolled her forward a bit and hit the clutch and brakes, and as I was stopping, there was some screeching in the brakes.  I don't know if it's wet or the brakes are worn.  (I think it's wet but wanted to ask anyway).  The two ladies looked at me when I stopped so I know it's loud.  (I can't hear anything [hearing loss]).  I'll try driving her some more in a little after I shower.<P>(It wasn't screeching when moving quick but only at like 5 kph and under)<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ferrari_cdn" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrari_2.JPG"> </A>  <BR>'84 2m4, 4 speed, 106k miles (157k km)  AIM: CanadianFiero||||reg||4
Z||000001||Ferrari_cdn||10-06-2001||05:52 PM||||Oh one more thing, that wasn't the only thing that happened.  The CHECK ENGINE light did come on.  (for 5 seconds) then went off.  Something up with the engine or all the water down the vents could have caused that?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ferrari_cdn||10-06-2001||06:05 PM||||Ok nevermind the brakes.  I was getting paranoid.  Anyway I took her out and tried to play with the brakes.  It WAS the wet calipers and rotors that screeched.  (I was hosing the tires).  I went around the block twice and no screeching happened.<P>The only thing now bugs me is the CHECK ENGINE thingy that came on for 5 seconds.  Oh well.||||reg||7
